    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are proud to introduce 60 Hunter's Hall to the market. This spacious and well-presented one-bedroom apartment is ideally situated on the ground floor and benefits from its own private hall door and patio, giving it a wonderful sense of independence and privacy. With no onward chain and currently vacant, the apartment is ready for immediate occupancy. \n\nThe well-designed accommodation comprises an inviting entrance hallway, a generous open-plan kitchen and living area, a good-sized double bedroom and a family bathroom. The apartment enjoys an abundance of natural light throughout, creating a bright and welcoming environment, while the private patio and own-door access further enhance the sense of having a space entirely your own.\n\nTucked away within the peaceful and sought-after Hunterswood development, No. 60 enjoys a convenient setting close to a wide range of local amenities, including shopping facilities, sports clubs and recreational amenities. The area is also well connected, with easy access to the M50 motorway and a number of bus routes providing convenient links to Dublin City Centre. This attractive apartment will appeal to first-time buyers, those looking to downsize, and investors alike, offering comfortable accommodation with the added benefit of privacy and a real sense of independence."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Exceptional property in a prime location in great condition</li><li> \"Own door\" apartment, with private patio to front</li><li> Conveniently close to a wide range of amenities, including M50, N7, and more</li><li> Expansive floor-to-ceiling windows, filling the space with natural light</li><li> Built-in wardrobes for ample storage</li><li> Peaceful, well-maintained development</li><li> Managment fee - approx. 1,700 per annum</li><li> Available for immediate occupancy, being vacant and free from any onward chain</ul>"
      },
      {
